    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Ты сейчас серьёзно?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Are you serious right now?' You'll hear 'you' all the time in the show, here connected with 'seriously'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, я абсолютно серьёзна.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, I am completely serious.' Notice the word order: 'I' comes first, and 'serious' finishes the sentence. Then Kostya replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Я этого не ожидал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I did not expect this.' The key word here means 'I', which Kostya combines with 'that'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Тебе следовало этого ожидать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You should have expected it.' You'll hear 'for you' all the time in the show, here connected with 'to expect'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Вчера всё было так хорошо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yesterday everything was so good.' The key word here means 'yesterday', which Kostya combines with 'was'. And Nastya jumps in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вчера осталось в прошлом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yesterday is in the past.' Nastya starts with 'yesterday' and pairs it with 'was left' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Что ты хочешь от меня?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What do you want from me?' You'll hear 'what' all the time in the show, here connected with 'me'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я хочу серьёзных отношений.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I want a serious relationship.' Notice the word order: 'I' comes first, and 'relationships' finishes the sentence. Kostya answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Я очень стараюсь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am trying my best.' The first content word means 'I', and 'try' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Этого недостаточно, Костя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It is not enough, Kostya.' A compact expression built around 'that' and 'Kostya'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Ты больше...",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You are not...' Kostya starts with 'you' and pairs it with 'more' to make the point clear. Then Nastya replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Не что?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Not what?' Nastya puts 'what' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'what'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Ты не счастлива со мной?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
